; onehotr_sample_charged_nothing: ONEHOTR on a sample register is
; charged nothing, so the type check decides the fault at any budget.
;
; spec/xqvm/SPEC.md ("A charge sized from the register reads it only as a
; model") sizes the ONEHOTR charge from the row extent of a model register
; and makes it zero for any other value. The sample below is nine binary
; variables (72 bytes at the variable rate) under a budget of exactly 72,
; resized to a 3x3 grid, and row 0 is in range. Charging the row's
; three variables would cost equality_expansion_bytes(3) = 3x32 + 3x48 =
; 240 bytes and raise MemoryLimitExceeded; charging nothing leaves only
; the type check, which raises TypeMismatch for a model-only opcode on a
; sample.
;
; QUI-1500: this vector is the pin on this behaviour.

PUSH 9
BSMX r0          ; a 9-variable binary sample: 72 bytes, the whole budget
PUSH 3
PUSH 3
RESIZE r0        ; 3x3 grid; RESIZE accepts model|sample
PUSH 0           ; row, in range
PUSH 1           ; penalty
ONEHOTR r0
HALT
